In this archive is version 0.06a of Quip, the 'fortune'ish program.  It
will work on any Amiga with enough memory to hold the program itself and
the standard disk buffer (and maybe 3*64k, depending on what options you
choose to use).

It's not pretty, but it does the job.

You should have the following files:

quip                       23756 bytes
quip.doc                   18502 bytes

Quip requires a datafile to work.  While they are easy enough to create, a
seperate archive (quipdat.lha) should have one that will do well.  The
directions explain how to add new quips to your datafile (and sorta how to
create a new one).  Read it carefully.

- Trey
